# Project-local act configuration. Composes with ~/.actrc.
# Globals (runner images, --bind, --artifact-server-path, credentials) come
# from ~/.actrc; this file adds project-specific overrides only.
#
# `make act-init` bootstraps .act.{vars,env,secrets} from the .example files.
#
# -W pins act to ci.yml. publish.yml is deliberately excluded: act has no OIDC
# and ignores job.permissions, so it cannot run the publish jobs meaningfully
# and would fail in a way that looks like a workflow bug.

# act's artifact server binds a FIXED port (34567) from a global default, so two act
# runs anywhere on this machine collide with "bind: address already in use" — and it
# starts even for a workflow that uses no artifacts, merely because ~/.actrc sets
# --artifact-server-path. Port 0 lets the OS pick a free one, so a local replay here is
# immune to other sessions replaying their own CI at the same time.
--artifact-server-port 0

--var-file .act.vars
--env-file .act.env
--secret-file .act.secrets
-W .github/workflows/ci.yml
